<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 20032 0 R/Alt(Block diagram. A dashed rectangle is the block. On the left outside, an external register drives logic that enters the block at an input port. Inside, logic leads to register A, more logic to register B, and more logic to an output port. Outside on the right, logic leads to a second external register. A second row inside the block connects a second input port through logic straight to a second output port. Labels 1 to 4 mark the path from the input to register A, from register A to register B, from register B to the output, and from the second input to the second output. Arrows above the outside parts are labeled input delay and output delay.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 29988 0 R>>
